    "Vertebrates are animals with a backbone: a column of small bones, the vertebrae, around the nerve cord, part of an internal skeleton. There are five main groups.",
    "Mammals have hair or fur, feed their young on milk from mammary glands, give birth to live young after internal fertilisation, breathe with lungs, and keep a constant body temperature. Their teeth come in different types.",
    "Birds have feathers, and their front limbs are wings. A beak with no teeth; lungs; hard-shelled eggs; a constant body temperature. Scales on the legs are a reminder that birds are close to reptiles.",
    "Reptiles have dry scales, breathe with lungs, and lay eggs with a leathery waterproof shell on land after internal fertilisation. Their body temperature follows the surroundings.",
    "Amphibians have smooth, moist skin without scales. They lay soft eggs in water, where the young (tadpoles) breathe with gills; adults breathe with lungs and through the skin. Body temperature follows the surroundings.",
    "Fish have wet scales, fins, and gills all their lives. They lay soft eggs in water after external fertilisation, and a lateral line along each side senses movement in the water.",
