    "Arthropods are animals with jointed legs, a body in segments, and a hard outer skeleton — the exoskeleton — which must be shed (moulted) for the animal to grow. More than three-quarters of all known animal species are arthropods.",
    "Insects: three body parts — head, thorax, abdomen; three pairs of jointed legs, on the thorax; usually two pairs of wings; one pair of antennae; compound eyes.",
    "Arachnids: two body parts — cephalothorax and abdomen; four pairs of legs; no antennae and no wings; simple eyes, usually eight.",
    "Crustaceans: two body parts; more than four pairs of legs, the front pair often claws; two pairs of antennae; gills, and most live in water.",
    "Myriapods: a body of many similar segments, each with jointed legs — one pair per segment in centipedes, two pairs in millipedes; one pair of antennae; no wings.",
    "The quick way: count the legs. Six, an insect; eight, an arachnid; ten or more on a two-part body, a crustacean; many, on a body of repeated segments, a myriapod."
